---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About our Phoenix developer meetups"
  description="Get to know Code Coffee Break, a developer community in Phoenix, Arizona for exploring AI agents, building projects, and sharing ideas over coffee."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>Learn and build with other developers.</h1>
      <p>Small gatherings around code, AI agents, and coffee.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="page-body">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>Meet in person, work on something real</h2>
        <p>
          Code Coffee Break is being built around small, in-person developer
          meetups in Phoenix, Arizona. Bring a project, explore an AI coding workflow, ask for help,
          or share something you learned.
        </p>
        <p>
          The first gathering is in planning. The date and venue are not yet
          confirmed, and registration is not open. Developers at any stage are welcome.
        </p>
        <h2>Examples you can inspect</h2>
        <p>
          The opening articles are original, AI-assisted editorial pieces. They
          use fictional scenarios, source links, and runnable examples where
          appropriate. They are not accounts of personal projects or production
          incidents. Each article identifies its authorship and any illustrative
          data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Future contributors keep their own bylines. Measurements need a
          method; external claims need a source. Corrections should explain what
          changed.
        </p>
        <h2>Room for other voices</h2>
        <p>
          Resources support the conversations between meetups. The{' '}
          <a href="/contribute">contribution guide</a> is ready; submissions are
          not open yet. There are no invented members, event schedules, or
          audience numbers.
        </p>
        <h2>Keep it simple</h2>
        <p>
          Read without an account. Try the <a href="/tools">browser tools</a>{' '}
          without uploading your inputs. Follow new writing through{' '}
          <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>. See the <a href="/#next-meetup">meetup page</a>
          for the first gathering's status.
        </p>
      </article>
      <Newsletter />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
